WEBVTT

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.320
Hihara-sempai.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.540
I'm sorry about yesterday!

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.120
Huh?

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.310
No. I left you with such a bad memory.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.090
Are you gonna pull off your second selection?

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.270
Huh?

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.930
Are you for real,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.090
or are you a fraud?

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.100
The Secret Duet

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.750
I can't concentrate.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.970
What did he mean by that?

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:21.720
Are you for real,

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.390
or are you a fraud?

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.460
Could he have found out about my magic violin?

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:32.420
That's a magic violin. Anyone can play it.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.290
I'm going to give it all I have, so please play well for me.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.970
Why am I talking to it?!

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.640
Ah, geez!

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.490
I'm thirsty.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.780
You look pretty free, Hino.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.580
Kanazawa-sensei!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.340
I'm taking a break. It's not that I have free time.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.910
There'll be plenty of time for breaks.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.600
Let's go, Hino.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.880
Huh? But, uh, what...

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.540
I appreciate this a lot.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.420
In the meantime, once we finish grocery shopping, let's load it into the car,

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.200
and then go look at some souvenirs.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.160
No, we should be thanking you for all you're doing for us.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.970
But, Sensei, why did you choose us to carry your bags?

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.290
Wouldn't the boys be better at this?

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:42.140
Fuyuumi and Shimizu said they wanted to go souvenir shopping, and then I spotted you.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.750
Good timing, don't you think?

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.490
Good timing?

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.160
What's up, Tsukimori?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.070
"We're out shopping for dinner, so please watch the house. Lunch is on the table, heat it on the stove. - Kanazawa"

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.080
Shopping for dinner?

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.700
Seems like it.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.000
When did they head out?

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:04.100
"Lunch is on the table, heat it on the stove," huh?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:09.770
The it's just you, me, Hihara-sempai, and Yunoki-sempai left behind, huh?

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:14.550
I'll go look for them. You heat up the food, OK?

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.880
I'm counting on you, Tsukimori.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.800
Those are so cute, Fuyuumi-chan!

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.830
They're cookies. My mom likes them, so she asked me to pick them up for her.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.790
Yeah? Maybe I should buy some to take home, too.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.790
What are you buying, Shimizu-kun?

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.710
Teacups.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.240
Yeah, that has souvenir written all over it.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:46.720
It's for my mother and father, but I'm not sure which one to get.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.440
Gotcha.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.340
In that case, get one with a prettier color.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:58.010
Sempai, were you practicing in the garden today?

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:01.070
You heard me? I must have sounded awful.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.660
Yes, very.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.690
Well, it is the truth.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.990
Shimizu-kun, how much do you practice each day?

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:13.950
I play whenever I feel like playing.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:19.380
I'm not sure how many hours it is, but often by the time I realize it, the sun is up.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.590
What?!

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:26.320
When I'm playing, and my fingers are moving along gracefully, it sounds nice.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.100
It makes me so happy.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:37.810
It makes me wish I could play those ideal notes at any time.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.710
Ideal... notes?

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:46.660
But the only way to do that is by practice, huh?

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:52.870
I wonder if I'll be able to play those ideal notes he's talking about someday.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:58.400
I can't rely on my magic violin forever.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.840
I need to practice more and raise my skills

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.660
so I can get closer to being the real thing.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.200
Huh? Why is Tsuchiura cooking?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.180
I thought they said the food was cooked already.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.380
But, wow, Tsuchiura can cook! Awesome!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.340
Tsukimori.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.560
I said I'm sorry.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.520
All you had to do was heat it up on the stove,

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.780
so how did it come out like that?!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.850
I got it confused with the oven. It can't be helped.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.490
You call that an apology?!

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.710
Chow time!

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.160
This is delicious!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.880
Tsuchiura, you're a genius!

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.510
That's too much. It's just fried rice.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.440
No, you really are!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.180
You can cook and play the piano, too!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:51.570
It's a bit late to say now, but I was surprised when I heard you were entering the competition.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.050
You've played piano since you were a kid, huh?

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.330
Oh, yes, that's true.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.590
Speaking of piano,

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:03.590
I've been to one of Tsukimori-kun's mother's recitals before.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:04.660
My mother?

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.720
Tsukimori's mother?

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.080
She's Misa Hamai-san, the pianist.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.540
Misa Hamai?! I've heard of her!

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.380
You serious? Both mother and son...?

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.550
Yeah.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:20.940
Her piano playing has this soft tone to it, full of sentiment...

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.460
It feels completely different from the way you play.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.750
Could you stop talking about my family?

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:30.220
It's a nuisance to have people get all curious about it.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.870
Sorry.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:33.860
Tsuchiura?

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.060
I'll go get some tea.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.460
Count me in!

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.860
But your mother really is a lovely pianist.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.570
Thank you very much.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.120
Tea, tea!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:56.820
Ah, nothing like a mouthful of tea after eating!

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.760
Hihara-sempai, that's...

00:07:58.760 --> 00:07:59.500
Huh?

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.750
Hino

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.580
Hey, Hino, don't try to carry too much!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.410
OK! I'm all right!

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.230
You're not all right, are you?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.230
You're not all right, are you?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.620
Geez! You startled me!

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:17.470
Sorry.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.180
My bad.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:21.360
Hino-chan, the truth is...

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:22.340
Yes?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.800
I'm sorry! I spilled all the tea from your plastic bottle!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.460
That's fine, really.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.030
But why?

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.590
Hihara-sempai?

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:40.790
Uhh... Oh, I should take this to the kitchen, huh? Here I go!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:41.330
Bye!

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.070
The kitchen!

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.480
Did something happen?

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.410
Who knows.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.410
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.570
Hmm?

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.810
Sorry about yesterday.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.050
I should have cleaned up.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.430
Don't worry about it.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:04.400
Also, if you could, I'd like you to forget that incident...

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:07.800
Huh?

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.350
I-It's nothing!

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.740
If...

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:23.670
If everyone found out about the magic violin...

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.590
I wonder what would happen.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:41.800
The son of a musician really is on a different level.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:44.340
Such technique... He's a virtuoso.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:46.120
I wonder if he takes after his father.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.900
It's gotta be in his genes.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:50.450
Len,

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:54.860
music is something you both enjoy and make others enjoy, too.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:59.310
Do you understand? It's not just about technique.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:04.740
Their music is genuinely sweet...

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.960
And gentle...

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:15.750
I fell asleep, huh?

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:39.810
Yes.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.870
Their music...

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.060
...is genuinely...

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.570
...heartwarming.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.900
Didn't that sound lovely to you right now,

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.880
Tsukimori-kun?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.270
Huh?

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:06.790
Tsukimori-kun!

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:09.740
Tsukimori-kun...

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.880
Welcome back, Tsukimori-kun.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:21.740
Those violins were you and Hino-san, weren't they?

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:30.040
It was a rather nice performance,

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:34.600
but... it didn't sound like you.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.240
Thanks for letting us stay here!

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.600
No, feel free to stop by any time.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.430
Got everything, guys?

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.190
We're good to go, Kanayan.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.370
By the way, Kanazawa-sensei,

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.370
when were you going to tell us the theme for the second selection?

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.670
You promised you'd tell us on the final day here, right?

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.490
Oh, yeah? I completely forgot about it.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:03.550
What?!

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.260
That was a joke.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:10.500
OK, I will now tell you the theme for the second selection.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.610
The theme is:

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.450
"Something to Believe In."

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:17.670
Something to believe in...

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:21.110
Something to believe in...

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:58.060
Hey, did you hear?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:02.120
Tsukimori-kun's parents were invited to the next selection.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.880
They're getting special treatment.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:07.810
When it comes to sheer ability, he's the clear favorite to win.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:09.860
Tsukimori-kun.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:11.450
Kyoto-sensei...

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.010
It's about the second selection...

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:16.420
I know your mother is in the middle of performing overseas,

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.840
but I was wondering if she could make it?

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.540
Yes, she sent a letter saying she'll be arriving a day earlier.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:25.590
Great. I'm looking forward to the second selection.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:38.170
Practicing during lunch again?

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:39.680
Yeah. You too?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.690
Yeah.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:46.200
Supposedly she didn't even pick up a violin until she entered the competition.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:50.500
When I heard that, I was shocked myself.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:54.340
For a girl like that to exist, she must be...

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:56.470
A virtuoso.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.620
Is everything OK?

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:04.000
This may be sudden, Hino-san,

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.050
but when did you start playing the violin?

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.280
Huh?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:13.050
I heard you just started, but I wanted to know if that's true.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:16.010
W-Well...

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.830
Ah! There you are!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.230
Geez!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.690
Don't run off in the middle of a conversation, Tsukimori-kun!

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:23.710
Amo-san.

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.140
You were asking me all these dumb questions.

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:29.850
I want a comment from the first selection's victor!

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:32.330
I'd also like to ask a little about your family...

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.640
I'm under no obligation to talk to you.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.330
Hey! Tsukimori-kun!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.860
Geez...

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:42.730
Hino-san!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:43.570
Yes?

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:46.570
I guess I could use a comment from another participant.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:47.250
What?!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.280
What happened to your accompanist?

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.910
Why did Tsuchiura-kun fill in as her replacement?

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:54.220
Oh, and since when did he play the piano?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.990
How did you guys get to be so close if you're in different classes?

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:02.410
Oh, Amo-san. Look, Yunoki-sempai!

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:05.600
Oh, Yunoki-sempai, huh?

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:08.370
He's surrounded, as usual.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.410
He's smart, attractive, and well kempt.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.160
He's got a million dollar smile and is incredibly popular.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:16.460
There's not a bad rumor about him, he's the picture of an honor student.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.760
He's, how can I put this...

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.910
He's too perfect. It's suspicious.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.080
Huh?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.370
Oh, sorry, sorry! Forget that!

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.210
But, Hino-san...

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.810
Before the first selection, you didn't seem to be interested in all this,

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.310
but now you're working really hard.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.000
I've changed my opinion of you.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:42.820
That kinda... makes me feel happy.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.200
Tsukimori! Tsukimori!

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.310
Why are you off in La-La Land?

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:52.050
All right, I'm taking off!

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:54.450
Must be tough having famous parents.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:56.920
But I guess it has its perks, too.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.030
Tsukimori-kun!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.770
I'd love your cooperation.

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:08.370
I'd like to ask about your family...

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.140
My family?

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:12.670
Let's see... Your father was a violinist and he's the president of an instrument manufacturer,

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.640
and your mother...

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.040
If you want to know about my family, go ask them directly.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:17.710
Umm... Hey!

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:19.180
Wait!

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.790
Tsukimori-kun!

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.850
Geez!

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.550
Ah, I wonder why...

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:57.030
It sounded so lovely the night I played along with Tsukimori-kun,

00:17:57.030 --> 00:17:59.970
but now I can't get that same sound out again...

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.110
How you doing, Kahoko Hino?

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:03.970
Lili!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.030
I'm not improving as much as I thought I'd be...

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:08.770
That's not true.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:12.060
You've improved a ton, compared to when you started.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.030
Y-Yeah?

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.430
I want you to keep working as hard as you are.

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:21.160
Though, it was sort of disappointing that you finished last in the first selection...

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.780
The rank is irrelevant.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:25.050
Didn't you say all you wanted was for me to enter?

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:28.870
Whatever do you mean?

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.090
I-I'm kidding! It's a joke!

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:38.250
Of course, I'm OK with just you entering!

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.010
Geez.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:45.250
But, I do need to hurry and choose a piece to play.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.290
I need to find an accompanist, too.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:51.780
I'm gonna head home. I'm exhausted,

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.840
and hungry...

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:56.250
I wonder what's for dinner...

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:05.870
Huh?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.790
Tsukimori-kun!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.070
Excuse me!

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.290
Huh? What's going on?

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.480
Hey, Tsukimori-kun!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.880
Where did you run off to?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.950
Wh-What?

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.850
Hold on!

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:28.300
Huh? No! Be still, my beating heart!

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:31.470
Huh? That's weird.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:35.620
Where did he run off to?

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.850
I'm sorry.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:46.590
What was that all about?!

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:49.690
Hino-san, are you going to keep using this practice room?

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.540
I was actually about to go home...

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.490
Then, let me use it after you.

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:57.640
Could you pack up your things and leave?

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:00.030
Well, excuuuse me!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:04.900
What's with him? What's with him? What's with him?!

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:08.160
He could have been a little kinder about it!

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.110
Geez, my face is still hot!

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.190
Hot?

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.180
Even if I go back there,

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:21.150
he'll just ream me out for interfering with his practice again, huh?

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:28.880
It might just be my imagination...

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:31.600
It might just be my imagination, but...

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:39.630
The last time I felt Tsukimori-kun's hand, it was so cold,

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.830
and today it was hot like it was burning.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.420
Tsukimori-kun!

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.310
Tsukimori-kun, can you hear me?

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.680
I'll go get the doctor. Just wait here.

00:20:57.790 --> 00:20:58.720
Stop.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:02.450
I don't need you to take care of me. It just gets in my way.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:04.970
This isn't the time for that!

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:06.920
Let go of me, Tsukimori-kun!

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:12.390
Tsukimori-kun...

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:39.720
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:39.710
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:44.730
Kahoko Hino and Len Tsukimori played together today, didn't they?

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:48.470
When two people perform together like this, it's called an instrumental duo,

00:23:48.470 --> 00:23:50.510
or in other words, a duet.

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:54.510
The previous performance where Kazuki Hihara played the trumpet was also a duet.

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:56.660
If it's three people, it's called a trio.

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:59.280
And four people is called a quartet.

00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:01.210
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:05.110
What do you call it when five people perform together?

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:09.650
Next Episode

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:09.560
You only realize the importance of something once it's broken.

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:12.980
It's OK! There's nothing that can't be repaired after being broken!

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:15.550
Hihara-sempai, I'd beg to differ. I broke it.

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:18.160
Next episode: The Heart-spun Canon.

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:20.100
Ah! I've done it!

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:21.940
The answer is...

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:25.100
A quintet!
